From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: skip the user-PD stop handshake when the firmware is gone

ath11k_ahb_stop_user_pd() always sends the SMP2P stop request and waits
ATH11K_USERPD_STOP_TIMEOUT for an ack from the firmware that spawned the
user PD. After a fatal error on the Q6 that firmware no longer exists, and
ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH stays set until a recovery actually brings it back -
it is what makes every WMI command fail with -ESHUTDOWN in the meantime.

The ack can then never arrive, so the stop burns its full five-second
timeout, twice on this board, and the -ETIMEDOUT return skips the SCM
power-off and the MSA unprepare. The teardown finishes with pending ack
frames still queued, and ieee80211_free_hw() warns on the way out:

  ath11k c000000.wifi: UserPD stop wait timed out
  Have pending ack frames!
  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 12722 at net/mac80211/main.c:1716
    ieee80211_free_ack_frame+0x58/0x60 [mac80211]
    ieee80211_free_hw+0x30/0x470 [mac80211]
    ath11k_mac_destroy+0x50/0x84 [ath11k]
    ath11k_core_deinit+0x124/0x180 [ath11k]
    ath11k_ahb_remove+0x78/0xc0 [ath11k_ahb]

Measured on the RD03v2 bench (IPQ5018 + QCN6122) with one 2.4 GHz assert
and the watchdog's driver reload: crash detected at 94529.4, the root PD
back up at 94531.7, the 5 GHz stop timing out at 94570.9 and the 2.4 GHz
one at 94579.5, the warning immediately after.

Skip the handshake while CRASH_FLUSH is set and tear the user PD down
locally instead. Behaviour on a healthy stop is unchanged: the flag is only
set by the crash-reconfigure path, and it is cleared once a recovery
succeeds.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -579,25 +579,41 @@
 
 	ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: power-down begin id=%d stop_done=%d\n",
 		    ab_ahb->userpd_id, completion_done(&ab_ahb->userpd_stopped));
-	reinit_completion(&ab_ahb->userpd_stopped);
-	ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop request assert\n");
-	ret = qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state, BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit),
-					 BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit));
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ab_ahb->userpd_stopped,
-						ATH11K_USERPD_STOP_TIMEOUT);
-	ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop wait end remaining=%lu\n",
-		    time_left);
-	ret = qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state,
-					 BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit), 0);
-	ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop request cleared\n");
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-	if (!time_left) {
-		ath11k_warn(ab, "UserPD stop wait timed out\n");
-		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+
+	/*
+	 * This stop request is an SMP2P handshake answered by the firmware that
+	 * spawned this user PD. After a fatal error on the Q6 that firmware is
+	 * gone, and ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH stays set until a recovery really
+	 * brings it back - it is what makes every WMI command fail with
+	 * -ESHUTDOWN meanwhile. The ack can then never arrive: the wait below
+	 * would only burn its five-second timeout, and its -ETIMEDOUT return
+	 * skips the SCM power-off and the MSA unprepare, leaving the pending ack
+	 * frames that make ieee80211_free_hw() warn on the way out. Tear the
+	 * user PD down locally instead, as qcom_q6v5_mpd does for a dead root PD.
+	 */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags)) {
+		ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: firmware is gone; skipping the stop handshake\n");
+	} else {
+		reinit_completion(&ab_ahb->userpd_stopped);
+		ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop request assert\n");
+		ret = qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state, BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit),
+						 BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit));
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ab_ahb->userpd_stopped,
+							ATH11K_USERPD_STOP_TIMEOUT);
+		ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop wait end remaining=%lu\n",
+			    time_left);
+		ret = qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state,
+						 BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit), 0);
+		ath11k_info(ab, "rd03v2 userpd trace: stop request cleared\n");
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		if (!time_left) {
+			ath11k_warn(ab, "UserPD stop wait timed out\n");
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10) {
